I’ve traced six PPC store-call families; they all use the same clamping dispatcher for this register. `stfd` submits eight bytes, but the callback receives four at the register base. V3 needs a qualification: the OR expression also uses a signed `int`, so upper bits are not provably zero—but under the sign-extension behavior you describe, they appear only when bit 31 is already set.
